{#
  The pi-peer-backup CronJob's exported verdict: annotations on this object, patched by the script
  each nightly run (files/pull-pi-peers.sh:export_verdict), exported by kube-state-metrics as
  kube_configmap_annotations and read by the shadow rules in observability's `pods` group (M6
  batch B7, docs/target-architecture/monitoring/m6-retire-kuma.md).

  DECIDED: rendered with no annotations, so the annotations have one writer. The object must
  exist before the first run, because RBAC cannot narrow `create` by name and the CronJob's Role
  grants `patch` on this one name only. With no annotation in the render, Ansible's client-side
  apply records none in its last-applied annotation, and a Flux server-side apply owns none, so
  neither removes or reverts what the script wrote. This is the field-ownership argument
  configarr's verdict ConfigMap rests on (configarr/templates/health-verdict-configmap.yaml.j2).
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ pi_peer_backup_k8s_verdict_configmap }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
  labels:
    app: pi-peer-backup
